## {{lb|en|southwest|_|England}} To [[cut#Verb|cut]], [[scratch#Verb|scratch]], or [[tear#Verb|tear]] (someone or something) with a [[sharp#Adjective|sharp]] [[object#Noun|object]]; to [[lacerate#Verb|lacerate]], to [[slash#Verb|slash]]; specifically {{lb|en|nautical}}, to [[make#Verb|make]] [[mark#Noun|marks]] on (something, such as a [[piece#Noun|piece]] of [[wood#Noun|wood]]) [[use#Verb|using]] a [[race knife]].
##* {{RQ:Ascham Toxophilus|edition=new|folio=38|passage=Buckles and agglettes at vnwares, ſhall '''race''' his bowe, a thinge both euill for the fight, ⁊ perillous for freatinge.}}
##* {{RQ:Markham Cavelarice|book=7|chapter=Of Paine in the Teeth, and of the Woolfes|page=54|passage=Paine in a horſſes teeth commeth either from pride and corruption of blood, or els from cold rhums, {{...}} the cure is, vvith a ſharp knife to '''race''' him alongſt his gummes, cloſe vnder his teeth, both of the inſide and outſide: and then to rubbe them all ouer, either vvith pepper & ſalt vvel mingled together, or vvith claret vvine and pepper heated vpon the fire, {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:Moxon Mechanick Exercises|volume=I|subchapter=Of Locks and Keys|page=19|passage=Then ''File'' one edge very ſtraight by laying a ''ſtraight Ruler'' juſt vvithin the edge of it, and dravving or '''raceing''' vvith a point of hardned Steel a bright line by the ſide of the ''Ruler'': {{...}}}}
## {{lb|en|obsolete}}
### To [[alter#Verb|alter]] (a [[document#Noun|document]]) by erasing parts of it.
###* {{RQ:Palsgrave Lesclarcissement|book=3rd|chapter=The Table of Verbes|folio=cccxxxii|column=1|passage=This indenture is '''raced''' all the worlde may ſe it: ''Ceſte indenture eſt faulcée tout le monde le peult veoyr.''}}
###* {{RQ:Marlowe Nashe Dido|sig=A3|page=25|passage=But I vvill take another order novv, / And '''race''' th'eternall Regiſter of time: {{...}}}}
### To [[level#Verb|level]] or [[tear down]] (a [[building#Noun|building]], a [[town]], etc.) to the [[ground#Noun|ground]]; to [[demolish]].
###* {{RQ:Raleigh Mahomet|page=50|passage=For his further ſecuritie he {{quote-gloss|Don Roderigo}} diſarmed his ſubjects; ſuch Caſtles and ſtrengths as hee vvas jealous of vvere '''raced''', {{...}}}}
###* {{RQ:Swift Miscellanies|title=Nobles and Commons|chapter=Of the Dissensions in Athens, between the Few and the Many|page=29|passage={{...}} ''[[w:Lysander|Lyſander]]'' the General of the ''Lacedemonians'', {{...}} novv reduces all the Dominions of the ''Athenians'', takes the City, '''races''' their VValls, ruins their VVorks, and changes the Form of their Government; {{...}}|footer=Spelled ''razes'' in the 1st edition (1701), [https://books.google.com/books?id=diJZAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA20 page 20].}}
###* {{RQ:Grose England and Wales|volume=II|chapter=Leeds Castle, Kent|page=114|passage={{quote-gloss|{{w|Edward I of England}}}} cauſed [[w:Henry de Cobham, 1st Baron Cobham|Henry Cobham]], {{...}} to '''race''' the caſtle that Robert de Crevequer had erected, becauſe Crevequer (that vvas the ovvner of it, and heire to Robert) vvas of the number of the nobles that moved and mainteined vvare againſt him; {{...}}}}
### {{lb|en|rare}} To make (a [[path#Noun|path]] or [[way#Noun|way]]) through something by cutting or tearing.
###* {{RQ:Homer Chapman Iliads|book=XI|page=148|passage=[T]he king purſude / And furrovved through the thickned troopes. As vvhen tvvo chaced Bores / Turne head gainſt kennels of bold hounds, and '''race''' vvay through their gores: {{...}}}}
### {{lb|en|also|figurative}} To [[erase#Verb|erase]] (a [[record#Noun|record]], [[text#Noun|text]], etc.), originally by scraping; to [[rub out]], to [[scratch out]].
###* {{RQ:Wyatt Poems|poem=Sonnet 31|stanza=1|lines=13–14|page=43|passage=The wound alas happe in some other place, / From whence no toole away the skar can '''race'''.}}
###* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|year=1596.2|book=V|canto=IX|stanza=26|page=303|passage=Thus there he ſtood, vvhyleſt high ouer his head, / There vvritten vvas the purport of his ſin, / In cyphers ſtrange, that fevv could rightly read, / BON FONS: but ''bon'' that once had vvritten bin, / VVas '''raced''' out, and ''Mal'' vvas novv put in.}}
###* {{RQ:Heywood Fair Maid|page=38|passage=''Goodl''{{quote-gloss|''ack''}}. My name is Captaine ''Thomas Good——'' / ''Beſſ''{{quote-gloss|''e Bridges''}}. I can ſee no good in thee, '''Race''' that ſyllable / Out of thy name.}}
### {{lb|en|figurative}} To [[completely]] [[remove#Verb|remove]] (someone or something), especially from a [[place#Noun|place]], a [[situation#Noun|situation]], etc.; also, to remove from [[existence]]; to [[destroy]], to [[obliterate#Verb|obliterate]].
###* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=i|page=57|passage=VVithout reſpect of ſex, degree or age. / He '''raceth''' all his foes vvith fire and ſvvord.}}
###* {{RQ:Shakespeare Titus Andronicus Q1|act=I|scene=I|sig=C2|page=16|passage=Ile find a day to maſſacre them all, / And '''race''' their faction and their familie, {{...}}}}
### {{lb|en|clothing|footwear}} To make a [[cut#Noun|cut]] or [[slash#Noun|slash]] in (an [[item#Noun|item]] of [[clothing#Noun|clothing]] or [[footwear]]) as a [[decoration]].

