{{PIE word|en|wréh₂ds}}
From {{inh|en|enm|racen}}, {{m|enm|rasen|t=to come apart; to pick clean, strip; to pull away, snatch; to pull down, knock down; to pull off, strip off; to pluck or tear out; to tear apart}},<ref name="MED">{{R:MED Online|entry=rāsen|pos=''v.''(1)|noformat=1|id=MED35943}}</ref> either:<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=race|pos=''v.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=6091847023|date=July 2023}}</ref>

* an {{glossary|aphetic}} form of {{m|enm|arasen}}, {{m|enm|aracen|t=to pluck, pull, or tear away or out}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=arācen|pos=v|id=MED2063}}</ref> from {{der|en|xno|aracer}} and {{der|en|fro|aracier}}, {{m|fro|esracier}}, {{m|fro|esrachier|t=to pull off}} (modern {{cog|fr|arracher}}),<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=† arace|pos=v|id=2072439100|date=July 2023}}</ref> from {{der|en|la|ērādīcāre}}, the {{glossary|present}} {{glossary|active}} {{glossary|infinitive}} of {{m|la|ērādīcō|t=to root out; to annihilate, extirpate}}, from {{m|la|ē-}} (variant of {{m|la|ex-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘away; out’}} + {{m|la|rādīx|t=root}} (from {{der|en|ine-pro|*wréh₂ds|t=root}}) + {{m|la|-ō|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming regular first-{{glossary|conjugation}} {{glossary|infinitive}}s of {{glossary|verb}}s}}; or
* from {{der|en|xno|racer}}, an aphetic form of {{m|xno|aracer}} (see above).

