#* {{RQ:Ascham Toxophilus|edition=new|folio=30|passage=But nowe a ſtronge man not vſed to ſhoote, at a girde, can heue vp ⁊ plucke in ſunder many a good bowe, as wilde horſes at a brunt doth '''race''' and plucke in peeces many a ſtronge carte.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Richard 3 Q1|act=III|scene=ii|sig=G2|sigend=G2|versoend=1|page=59|passage=Stanley did dreame the boare did '''race''' his helme, / But I diſdaind it, and did ſcorne to flie, {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|year=1596.2|book=V|canto=V|stanza=11|page=242|passage=He to her lept vvith deadly dreadfull looke, / And her ſunſhynie helmet ſoon vnlaced, / Thinking at once both head and helmet to haue '''raced'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Warner Albions England|edition=5th|chapter=LXXIII|page=304|passage=Thus erring ''Rome'' hath, doth, & vvill our chriſtian VVorld [[unquiet|vnqueate]]: / May therefore Princes ioyne to '''race''' that Monſter from his Seate.}}

